# 02-ot-network/ot_protocol_outbound_to_external.rules
# A host inside HOME_NET opening a session to an industrial protocol port
# outside HOME_NET. The NCSC-led secure connectivity principles call for
# "Continuous monitoring of data flows within and between network segments",
# and AA25-343A asks owners to monitor outbound traffic at OT perimeter
# firewalls for "unexpected protocol usage". Controllers and HMIs have no
# reason to speak these protocols to the internet; an OT host doing so is
# either misconfigured or being used as a relay. Header, flow and threshold
# keywords only.
#
# Set HOME_NET to the OT ranges. Documented cross-boundary flows (for
# example an OPC UA client in the DMZ pulling from an OT server) arrive from
# outside and are not matched here; flows a site deliberately sends outward
# need a pass rule or a narrower HOME_NET.
#
# Linked from ICS-HUNT-0009.

alert tcp $HOME_NET any -> $EXTERNAL_NET [102,502,2222,2404,4840,20000,20256,44818] (msg:"ICS-DFIR OT host opened an industrial-protocol-port session to outside HOME_NET"; flow:established,to_server; threshold:type limit, track by_both, count 1, seconds 3600; reference:url,www.ncsc.gov.uk/sites/default/files/documents/ncsc-secure-connectivity-for-operational-technology.pdf; classtype:policy-violation; sid:9000014; rev:1;)
